=== ADDRESS CHECK MECHANISM ANALYSIS ===
Source: search/src/fetch/fetchPage.ts, lines 200-240

The foo.localhost rejection is NOT name-based. Analysis:
1. Lines 200-203: IP literals checked directly before connect
2. Lines 210-240: Hostname resolution via custom lookup hook
3. Line 224: ALL resolved records checked against isPublicAddress policy
4. If ANY record fails the policy check, connection is refused with "blocked_destination"

foo.localhost is resolved by the system resolver to [127.0.0.1, ::1]. Since both 127.0.0.1 and ::1
are in BLOCKED_V4 and BLOCKED_V6 (see addressPolicy.ts), the lookup rejects the entire host BEFORE
the socket connects.

Connect-time verification for non-special hostname resolving to loopback:
